  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/lxman/PdfLibrary",
  "published": "2026-07-30T01:52:52.777Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.5.2 fixes colour on the CMYK soft-proof path: a reserved process-name Separation or all-reserved DeviceN (e.g. [/Separation /Cyan ...]) now applies its process colourant DIRECTLY, ignoring the alternate's tint transform, in every painting context — fills, strokes, shadings, images and stencil masks (ISO 32000-2 8.6.6.4; matches Adobe). Previously such spaces flattened through their alternate, so a lying alternate painted the wrong plate. /None components still paint nothing and the RGB path is unchanged. Also: atomic file saves retry transient Windows locks instead of failing, and GetPageColorants logs when a malformed resource graph truncates its inventory. Remaining colour edge cases are each pinned by a baseline test — see Docs/colour/rendering-conformance.md (G-8 ... G-13). See CHANGELOG.md.\n\n2.5.0 adds a public embedded-files read API: PdfDocument.GetEmbeddedFiles() returns read-only EmbeddedFileDescriptor entries for the catalog's /Names /EmbeddedFiles name tree plus catalog-level /AF associated files (ISO 32000-2, 7.11.4 / 14.13) — names, file names, description, MIME subtype, associated-file relationship, and the decoded file bytes. Malformed content never throws; failing entries degrade to metadata-only. First consumer: Factur-X e-invoice extraction (factur-x.xml from PDF/A-3).\n\n2.4.0 adds a read-only conformance preflight (PDF/A-2b/2u/3b, PDF/X-4, PDF/UA-1) via PdfLibrary.Conformance.Preflighter, plus a CMYK / colour-managed rendering fidelity batch (Ghent Workgroup fixtures), 16-bit images, optional-content visibility, mesh shadings, a transparency-group render SPI, and text-extraction fixes. Additive and back-compatible. See CHANGELOG.md.",
